  "faq.title": "Questions people ask",
  "faq.1.q": "Does an AI decide the loan?",
  "faq.1.a": "No. Language models only read documents. A deterministic, versioned rule engine and a calibrated risk model decide, and every decision can be replayed exactly.",
  "faq.2.q": "Is this real customer data?",
  "faq.2.a": "No. Every applicant, statement and bureau record is synthetic. Accuracy figures describe a simulation. The adapters are shaped like the real feeds so they can be swapped in.",
  "faq.3.q": "What about informal income and messy statements?",
  "faq.3.a": "Income comes from twelve months of cash flow with a volatility haircut, so a salary slip is optional. Edited or window-dressed statements are caught by arithmetic and pattern checks.",
  "faq.4.q": "What if a data source is down?",
  "faq.4.a": "The case is referred to the Data queue and never guessed. Try it: in the application, step 4, simulate a bureau or KYC outage.",
  "faq.5.q": "How are fairness and privacy handled?",
  "faq.5.a": "Gender, religion and caste are never model inputs, and the simulator shows an adverse-impact check. Personal data is encrypted per case and can be erased by destroying its key.",
  "faq.6.q": "How would a lender plug this in?",
  "faq.6.a": "Through a REST API: submit an application, get a decision with evidence, call retry for counter-offers, and read the audit log. See the PS2 checklist page for the endpoint list.",
